<Base title="About">
  <article>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I write about physical capability, longevity, and the gap between what gets
      claimed and what survives checking.
    </p>
    <p>
      The through-line is a project I started years ago and keep rebuilding: a
      framework for what the body can actually be driven to do, and which of those
      gains hold up over decades. It began as a spreadsheet rating sports against
      athletic attributes. It is now closer to a research programme.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two commitments run through everything here. Evidence streams are kept separate
      and labelled &mdash; peer-reviewed findings, outlier cases, and practitioner
      knowledge each earn different kinds of confidence, and merging them quietly is
      how frameworks go wrong. And the corrections get published: every long document
      here has an audit section listing what did not survive verification, including
      my own earlier mistakes.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:angel.ivanov.raychev@gmail.com">angel.ivanov.raychev@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
